{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE15hamiltonianPath5Walks0E0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgyF","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Tours"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hamiltonianPath"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Path","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"title":"hamiltonianPath()","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Hamiltonian.swift#L555","fileName":"Hamiltonian.swift"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FindHamiltonianPath"},{"type":"text","text":"). Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches."}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath()"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hamiltonianPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Path","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","text":"Path"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exponential in the worst case (n! paths); O(degree) per step of the search,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus O(n + m) for the reachability test where it can fail (not after a step from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with no other unvisited neighbour, so a path or cycle graph takes O(n + m))."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/hamiltonianPath()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hamiltonianPath","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Path","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"title":"hamiltonianPath()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FindHamiltonianPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath()"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Walks/documentation/Walks/Path":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Path","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Path","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/walks\/path","abstract":[{"text":"A path: a walk that repeats no vertex, and so no edge (JGraphT’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"GraphPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", NetworkX’s simple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Path"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Path"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","title":"Vertex","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":